<title>USA: Tyco in stock offering to pay down debt.</title>
<headline>Tyco in stock offering to pay down debt.</headline>
<dateline>EXETER, N.H. 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tyco International Ltd said on Thursday it will sell 8.5 million shares of common stock under their existing effective universal shelf, and use the proceeds to repay acquisition-related debt.</p>
<p>The sale will increase the number of Tyco shares outstanding by 5 percent, to about 162.5 million.</p>
<p>The underwriters include Merrill Lynch &amp; Co, Credit Suisse First Boston, J.P. Morgan &amp; Co and Lehman Bros.</p>
<p>Tyco shares were down about a point to 58-1/2 in midday trading, after closing at 59-5/8 on Wednesday.</p>
<p>	  ((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
